From: MacSW maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] comctl32: Ignore HDM_LAYOUT when the HDLAYOUT is NULL or incomplete.

SOLIDWORKS 2026 sends HDM_LAYOUT with wParam = 0 and lParam = NULL to a
SysHeader32 control (sldimporttabu.dll, "set header height"). HEADER_Layout()
read lpLayout->pwpos without a check, so SLDWORKS.exe died with an access
violation (read of address 0x8) right after the License Agreement page.
Return FALSE instead of touching the structure. The caller ignores the result.

header.c is built into comctl32 v5 and v6, so both get the guard. Wine's own
senders (listview.c, winefile.c) always pass a valid HDLAYOUT, so their
behaviour does not change.

diff --git a/dlls/comctl32/header.c b/dlls/comctl32/header.c
index 2543e0a..dc4df5d 100644
--- a/dlls/comctl32/header.c
+++ b/dlls/comctl32/header.c
@@ -1495,6 +1495,9 @@ HEADER_InsertItemT (HEADER_INFO *infoPtr, INT nItem, const HDITEMW *phdi, BOOL b
 static LRESULT
 HEADER_Layout (HEADER_INFO *infoPtr, LPHDLAYOUT lpLayout)
 {
+    if (!lpLayout || !lpLayout->prc || !lpLayout->pwpos)
+        return FALSE;
+
     lpLayout->pwpos->hwndInsertAfter = 0;
     lpLayout->pwpos->x = lpLayout->prc->left;
     lpLayout->pwpos->y = lpLayout->prc->top;
